# SCRATCH BUILDS OF AN OLDER REVISION, written here and deleted again.
#
# Several tools measure a change against the build before it. devtools/harness
# `openDrive({rev})` now unpacks the revision's WHOLE client/ under
# node_modules/.cache/rev/<sha> (a main.ts alone beside the current siblings
# measured the old main.ts over the new roadsolve.ts, which is no control),
# but any test that needs a probe the old build lacks still grafts its own copy
# beside it (dock-sky, road-hole). Those live INSIDE client/ on purpose:
# main.ts imports ./menu and ./overlays by relative path and three from the
# repo's node_modules, so a copy bundled out of a temp directory resolves none
# of them.
#
# Each of them is a ~2MB stale duplicate of main.ts. They are removed in a
# `finally`, and that removal is the real guard — `cell-sync push` sends every
# file in the cell and does not read this file, so one left behind by a crashed
# run gets DEPLOYED as cell source. This keeps `git status` honest so the stray
# is visible while it exists, rather than committed by a tidy-up.
client/__rev-main.ts
client/__*-rev.ts
# A PROBE shim is the same thing: a copy of main.ts carrying extra window.__*
# so a measurement can reach a binding no shipped probe exposes. Two rules of
# its own, each learnt the hard way. It must be INSERTED before the file's
# last brace, never appended — main.ts's whole body is the else-clause of one
# `if (startLab(...))`, so code after it is module scope and sees none of the
# world's bindings (`kStore is not defined`, at the probe's first call). And
# it must NOT be a dotfile: tsconfig's include is `["client"]` and a wildcard
# include does not match a leading dot, so `client/.probe.ts` is never type
# checked and `tsc` passing is a check that could not fail. Name it to match
# the pattern above and both problems go away.
.DS_Store